# The Python sidecars are checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# They are not only run — they are ASSERTED ON as text: `denoise.rs` pulls
# `python/denoise.py` in with `include_str!` and pins protocol invariants by
# matching literal source, e.g. `"_reclaim_stale_parts(dest)\n    for attempt in"`.
# With `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default, and this machine's setting) a
# fresh clone would rewrite those newlines to CRLF and every such assertion would
# fail on a tree that is byte-identical in git. Pinning eol here makes the working
# copy match what the test expects, on any platform.
*.py text eol=lf
